{
  "name": "shrimp_boat_wreck",
  "version": 2,
  "introduced_by": "lowmouth",
  "notes": "A shrimp trawler sunk at her mooring, 15 m long and 4.5 m in the beam, settled in the mud so the deck is awash: a curved hull with a raised bow, a torn wheelhouse you can enter by the door in its aft wall (1 m by 2 m), a stove-in port bilge, a collapsed aft deck, a half-open fish hold and a leaning iron mast with one boom fallen. Bow to local -Z. Base sea.",
